# Product-runtime configuration template. Comments identify intended code consumers; they do
# not report which values are present in any live environment. Query live config and record
# unknowns as Unknown. Never commit secret values.
#
# #797: this file is now MACHINE-CHECKED against the code. packages/core/src/env-contract.ts is
# the declared contract (which variable, which service, required when, what shape), and
# env-contract.test.ts fails if this file, that contract, and the actual process.env reads in
# apps/ + packages/ ever disagree. Add a variable here and nowhere else → red. Read one in code
# and declare it nowhere → red. The boot check refuses to start a PRODUCTION process whose
# required or conditionally-required variables are missing, and rejects a malformed value in
# ANY environment (error messages name variables, never values).
#
# RAILWAY_GIT_COMMIT_SHA is deliberately absent below: the host injects it at deploy time and
# nothing here should ever set it. Web and worker each report it on the admin deploy-fingerprint
# row, so two services running different code are visible instead of merely surprising.

# ══════════════ CORE PRODUCT RUNTIME ══════════════
# Each variable is required only by the code path described below; this does not assert live use.

# ── Database (Neon) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev (docker compose up -d postgres):
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://fikirtive:fikirtive@localhost:5432/fikirtive"
# Neon production: direct URL here, -pooler URL below (runtime uses pooled).
# Historical evidence last observed a pre-pivot database name; the live name is Unknown until
# queried. Copy the exact URL from the authorized live console, never from this template.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://...@ep-xxx.neon.tech/<db>?sslmode=require"
# DATABASE_URL_POOLED="postgresql://...@ep-xxx-pooler.neon.tech/<db>?sslmode=require"
#   ↑ runtime MUST be the -pooler endpoint (PgBouncer). Under Prisma 7 driver-adapters
#     the app pool size is the pg Pool `max` set in code (packages/db/src/index.ts), NOT
#     the `connection_limit` URL param. Tune DB_POOL_MAX so (replica_count × max) stays
#     under Neon's pooled connection budget; defaults to 10/process when unset.
#     WORKER EXCEPTION (#796): the worker picks its own default ONLY for a role that raised
#     concurrency (today: WORKER_ROLE=wait) — 2 per concurrent job + 4 for timers. Leave it unset
#     there unless you have a replica-count reason not to. A value set BELOW that floor is kept
#     and warned about at boot, never overridden. An unset WORKER_ROLE touches nothing.
#     NOT THE WHOLE STORY: pg-boss opens its OWN pool too (default 10). Per-replica totals are
#     web 12, worker all/compute 20, worker wait 38 — see docs/ops/worker-services.md.
# DB_POOL_MAX="10"

# ── Worker services (#796 / #760) ────────────────────────────────
# One image, two Railway services.
#
# UNSET = "all" = byte-for-byte today's single service: every queue at concurrency 1, both
# connection pools left at their own defaults, reapers/scheduler/backup on, heartbeat row
# "worker". Raising concurrency is an explicit act, never a side effect of deploying.
#   WORKER_ROLE="compute"  → ingest / render / caption (ffmpeg, ffprobe, whisper). CPU-bound:
#                            in-process concurrency is fixed at 1; scale it with REPLICAS and a
#                            bigger container. This is the service to grow for heavier output.
#   WORKER_ROLE="wait"     → gen / refgen / research / publish (waiting on providers). THE ONLY
#                            role that raises concurrency. Also runs the reapers, the publish
#                            scheduler and the nightly backup.
# An unrecognised value EXITS at boot rather than guessing — apps/worker/src/plan.ts.
# The switch-over order matters (no overlapping supervision): docs/ops/worker-services.md.
# WORKER_ROLE="all"
#
# Per-queue JOB slots for the wait service (how many jobs run at once).
# GEN_CONCURRENCY="4"
# REFGEN_CONCURRENCY="2"
# RESEARCH_CONCURRENCY="2"
# PUBLISH_CONCURRENCY="2"
#
# The REAL provider ceiling — and it is NOT the job slots above. One image job fans out one paid
# request PER IMAGE (gen count ≤ 4, refgen ≤ 6), so those slots can mean up to 28 concurrent
# requests. This is the process-wide gate every paid request passes through, shared by gen and
# refgen (one account). Measured account ceiling: 10 concurrent requests (arkcli, 2026-08-08).
# Rule the boot log prints: replicas × PROVIDER_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS ≤ 8.
# PROVIDER_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS="6"
#
# WEB_BOOT_MIGRATION_STATUS — NOT for you to set. apps/web/scripts/boot.mjs writes it into the
# web process. When a boot migration did not apply, /api/ready returns 503 (so the platform keeps
# the previous deploy serving) while /api/health stays 200 and reports "migrations":"failed".
# Point the platform's DEPLOY/LOAD probe at /api/ready and its RESTART probe at /api/health.
# /api/health is ALWAYS 200 and never depends on the database — pointing a restart probe at an
# endpoint that fails when the DB fails is how a database blip becomes a web restart loop.

# ── Auth (Better Auth runtime contract; live enablement Unknown) ──
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=""                # openssl rand -base64 32 — apps/web/lib/better-auth/server.ts (also signs Meta OAuth state)
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3100"             # canonical origin — sessions + callbacks bind to it
NEXT_PUBLIC_BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3100" # browser client (public origin)
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""                  # Google OAuth app — apps/web/lib/better-auth/server.ts
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""
AUTH_ALLOWED_EMAILS="you@email.com"  # comma-separated allowlist (deny by default) — apps/web/lib/allowlist.ts
                                     # Since #543 this is the INVITE/back-door list, not the signup gate:
                                     # self-service registration admits its own address (AllowedEmail row,
                                     # invitedBy="self-signup"). Revoking a row still locks the account out.
# SIGNUPS_PAUSED="1"                 # emergency stop for NEW self-service signups — apps/web/lib/signup-gate.ts
                                     # Read live per request. FAIL-CLOSED: unset or 0/false/off/no keeps the
                                     # door open; ANY other value pauses it and /signup says so plainly.
                                     # Existing accounts, sign-in, magic link and password reset are unaffected.
FOUNDER_ADMIN_EMAILS="you@email.com" # comma-separated founder / super-admins (seeded to super-admin on sign-in)
# RESEND_API_KEY=""                  # production magic-link sender (resend.com) — apps/web/lib/better-auth/sender.ts
# AUTH_EMAIL_FROM="Fikirtive <auth@yourdomain.com>"  # verified Resend sender

# ── Token encryption (Meta OAuth tokens at rest) ─────────────────
# REQUIRED on BOTH web AND worker — @fikirtive/token-crypto throws without it (64 hex chars = 32
# bytes). Web encrypts the Meta token at OAuth-connect (apps/web/lib/token-encryption.ts); the
# publish WORKER decrypts it to publish (apps/worker/src/jobs/publish.ts decryptToken). Web and
# worker MUST carry the SAME value or the worker can't decrypt what the web app stored.
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""              # openssl rand -hex 32

# ── Signed media proxy (L1 organic publish — REQUIRED for publishing) ─────────
# The publish WORKER signs a short-lived HMAC token over (ownerId + storage key + expiry) and hands
# Meta a public URL (apps/worker/src/jobs/publish.ts signMediaToken); the WEB route verifies it and
# streams the private R2 bytes back (apps/web/app/api/media/pub/[token] verifyMediaToken). Web and
# worker MUST carry the SAME value — a mismatch makes every published post's media 404 at Meta →
# publish fails. Missing on either side = the whole L1 publish chain fails closed (posts never go
# out). Publishing requires the applicable platform approval; current approval status is Unknown
# until live-query. Configure each authorized environment before enabling publishing there.
# The worker also needs its media-proxy origin: PUBLIC_BASE_URL (or BETTER_AUTH_URL as fallback).
MEDIA_PROXY_SECRET=""                # openssl rand -hex 32 (web + worker share this exact value)
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL="https://app.fikirtive.com"  # worker-side public origin Meta fetches media from
#                                    # (apps/worker/src/jobs/publish.ts; falls back to BETTER_AUTH_URL)

# ── Share-preview links (B0-28 seat-less post review) ─────────────
# Web-only. Signs/verifies the HMAC share-preview token (apps/web/lib/schedule-actions.ts
# sharePostPreview + apps/web/lib/share-preview.ts verify). DELIBERATELY separate from
# MEDIA_PROXY_SECRET so the two capabilities can never be swapped. Missing = the share feature
# fails closed (mint returns an error; every share link 404s) — the rest of the app is unaffected.
SHARE_PREVIEW_SECRET=""              # openssl rand -hex 32

# ── Meta (Facebook/Instagram) app ────────────────────────────────
META_APP_ID=""                       # apps/web/lib/meta-graph.ts + /api/meta/authorize
META_APP_SECRET=""                   # also verifies data-deletion callbacks (/api/meta/data-deletion)
# The permission list is no longer sent on the authorize URL — it is packaged in the Meta dashboard
# under Facebook Login for Business → Configurations, and this is that configuration's ID.
META_LOGIN_CONFIG_ID=""              # apps/web/app/api/meta/authorize/route.ts

# ── Generation provider (SPEND) ───────────────────────────────────
# "mock" (default, $0), or "byteplus" (REAL money: Seedream image / Seedance video —
# the only paid provider, ADR 0003). Anything unrecognized resolves to the mock, so a
# misconfigured deploy can never silently burn money. Factory: packages/generation/src/index.ts.
# The provider selected in any live environment is external state; do not infer it here.
GENERATION_PROVIDER="mock"
# BYTEPLUS_API_KEY=""                # REQUIRED when GENERATION_PROVIDER=byteplus (Ark key, prefix ark-)

# ── Object storage (Cloudflare R2) ────────────────────────────────
# local (default): .data/storage on disk — dev only. A partial r2 config throws loudly
# (packages/storage/src/index.ts).
# #797: in PRODUCTION this is REQUIRED and must be "r2" — the boot check refuses to start a
# production process on local disk. Unset or "local" there means every merchant image and video
# is written to the container's own disk: gone at the next deploy, and web and worker each write
# to their own copy and cannot see each other's files. Locally, leave it unset.
# STORAGE_DRIVER="r2"
# R2_ENDPOINT="https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com"
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
# R2_BUCKET=""                      # exact environment bucket; changing a live bucket requires a separately approved, verified data migration

# ── Nightly DB backup: trigger + isolated credential (#794) ───────
# Docs: docs/runbooks/db-backup.md. Both blocks are set on the WORKER service.
#
# BACKUP_TRIGGER="cron"              # "cron" hands the nightly backup to the Railway cron
#                                    # service (start command: node apps/worker/dist/backup-cron.js).
#                                    # Anything else (incl. unset) keeps the legacy worker 5-min timer.
#                                    # Set it on BOTH the worker and the cron service so exactly
#                                    # one of them runs the backup.
#
# The backup writes under the `backups/` prefix. By default it reuses R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID above —
# which means one stolen app credential reaches BOTH the content and the backups that exist to
# survive losing it. Set the pair below to a separately minted, backup-scoped R2 token to break
# that. Both halves or neither: a half-set pair is a hard startup error, never a silent fallback.
# R2_BACKUP_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""         # backup-scoped R2 token (Cloudflare → R2 → Manage API tokens)
# R2_BACKUP_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
# R2_BACKUP_BUCKET=""                # optional — defaults to R2_BUCKET (same bucket, different key)
# R2_BACKUP_ENDPOINT=""              # optional — defaults to R2_ENDPOINT

# ── Stripe billing runtime config (live enablement Unknown) ───────
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""               # sk_live_… (Railway prod) / sk_test_… (dev) — apps/web/lib/stripe.ts
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""           # whsec_… — webhook signature IS the auth; wrong = all grants 400 (/api/stripe/webhook)

# ── Otto agent (LLM) — REQUIRED for the Otto loop ─────────────────
# Product runtime only. Sanitation/review/recovery/critique must not source or inject this key;
# any real provider/API spend requires explicit Founder approval.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""                 # read by @ai-sdk/anthropic inside packages/otto/src/model.ts
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=""              # optional gateway/proxy base URL
# OTTO_PROMPT_CACHE=""               # prompt-cache toggle — packages/otto/src/model.ts

# ── Otto research skill (web search) ──────────────────────────────
TAVILY_API_KEY=""                    # apps/worker/src/jobs/research.ts + apps/web/lib/otto-actions.ts
BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=""              # fallback search provider (same read sites)

# ════════════════ OPTIONAL / LOCAL-DEV ════════════════

# ── Auth wall toggle ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# In PRODUCTION the wall is ON unless explicitly set to "false" (fail-closed —
# a deploy that forgets it stays protected). In dev it is OFF unless set to "true".
AUTH_ENABLED="true"                  # apps/web/proxy.ts

# ── Who the rate limiters count (#795) ────────────────────────────
# Every per-caller gate (password door, the three public auth doors, magic link,
# signed media proxy) keys on the calling address. WHICH header carries a
# trustworthy address is a property of the deployment, so it is named here rather
# than guessed — apps/web/lib/caller-identity.ts.
#
#   railway    read X-Real-IP. Railway's edge sets it ("for identifying client's
#              remote IP", docs.railway.com/networking/public-networking/specs-and-limits)
#              and does NOT send X-Forwarded-For, so anything in that header on
#              Railway was written by the caller and is ignored.
#   xff:<hops> read X-Forwarded-For and count <hops> entries FROM THE RIGHT — for an
#              edge that appends (nginx, most CDNs). Entries are appended, so a caller
#              can only add on the left; <hops> must equal the number of trusted
#              proxies in front of the app. xff:1 = one edge.
#   dev        no proxy in front: take whichever of the two headers is present.
#              Local and CI only — "believe whichever header showed up" is exactly
#              the forgeable reading in production.
#
# Unset = "railway" in production (this product deploys there), "dev" elsewhere.
# CHECKED AT BOOT (apps/web/instrumentation.ts), not at the first request: an
# unrecognised value refuses to start, and so does "dev" in production — "dev"
# trusts whichever address header arrives, which lets any caller pick their own
# rate-limit bucket. Better Auth's own burst limiter reads the same authority
# (it is handed the resolved address in an internal header), so this one variable
# decides who BOTH limiters count.
# CALLER_IP_SOURCE="railway"         # railway | xff:<hops> | dev

# ── BytePlus resource-pack tracking (admin System Health) ─────────
# BYTEPLUS_RESOURCE_PACK_USD=""      # Total prepaid Seedance pack value on effective COGS basis, e.g. 35.64
# BYTEPLUS_RESOURCE_PACK_USED_USD="" # Optional console-read used amount; unset = admin estimates from frozen spend snapshots
# BYTEPLUS_RESOURCE_PACK_ALERT_PCT="20" # Admin System Health warns at or below this remaining percentage
# OTTO_DEFAULT_VIDEO_MODEL="seedance-2-mini"  # optional — the code fallback IS seedance-2-mini
#                                    # (2026-07-04: only flat margin-floored models are honored;
#                                    # a non-flat value degrades to seedance-2-mini with a warn).
# OTTO_LLM_MARGIN=""                 # LLM pricing margin override (default 2.0) — packages/core/src/llm-prices.ts
#                                    # MUST be >= 1.0. Below that every metered Otto turn and research
#                                    # run charges LESS than the provider's own bill (0.5 = sell at half
#                                    # cost), so the boot check refuses it and the runtime falls back to
#                                    # the default. 1.0 is the "never below cost" line, NOT the 45% margin
#                                    # floor — that one is judged per surface by scripts/check-margin-floor.mjs.

# ── Cowork vision ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# COWORK_VISION_ENABLED=""           # packages/core/src/cowork.ts — false is a HARD kill-switch the DB cannot countermand
# COWORK_VISION_MAX_IMAGES=""        # image cap (clamped in code)
# COWORK_VISION_MAX_BYTES=""         # byte cap (clamped in code)

# ── Worker extras ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FIKIRTIVE_DATA_DIR=""              # worker local storage root — apps/worker/src/storage.ts
# WHISPER_MODEL_DIR=""               # $0 caption job (whisper.cpp) — apps/worker/src/jobs/caption.ts
#                                    # DIRECTORY only: the model filename is derived in code, so
#                                    # this relocates the file and can never change the model.
# WHISPER_THREADS=""                 # whisper.cpp thread count
# WHISPER_MAX_SECONDS=""             # caption job duration ceiling
# R2_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=""             # "false" disables path-style (MinIO local verification)

# ── Runtime mode ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Normally set by the platform (the Dockerfiles set NODE_ENV=production). It is what turns the
# boot env check from "warn about missing variables" into "refuse to start".
# NODE_ENV="production"
# FIKIRTIVE_ENV_CONTRACT="warn"      # escape hatch: start a production process even though the
#                                    # contract check found problems. For the case where the CHECK
#                                    # is what is wrong — a launch gate must never be able to brick
#                                    # production with no way out. Default (unset) is enforce.

# ── Dev mocks / observability ─────────────────────────────────────
# META_GRAPH_MOCK=""                 # "1" serves canned Meta Graph responses — apps/web/lib/meta-graph.ts
# SENTRY_DSN=""                      # apps/web/instrumentation.ts + apps/worker/src/index.ts
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=""          # apps/web/instrumentation-client.ts — browser-side; Next.js
#                                    # inlines it into the client bundle at build time, so it is
#                                    # not a secret. Must be rebuilt (not just restarted) after
#                                    # changing it.
# APP_ORIGIN="https://app.fikirtive.com" # Meta data-deletion confirmation-page origin (falls back to request origin)
# /api/health (no auth) returns { ok, db, worker } — external monitors probe it;
# the worker heartbeats every 60s, 5 min without one = "stale". Wiring:
# docs/ops/incident-visibility.md.

# ── Generation queue metrics (admin Queue health, #779) ───────────
# Read-only. Unset = /admin/queue says "Not connected" and reads nothing (zero cost — the
# store bills on ingest volume, and this app never writes to it). Supplier-side queue
# observability ONLY; app/worker monitoring above coexists and is not replaced.
# QUEUE_METRICS_QUERY_URL=""         # full Prometheus-compatible query base, workspace path included
# QUEUE_METRICS_BASIC_AUTH=""        # "user:password" — omit when the endpoint needs no basic auth
# QUEUE_METRICS_PREFIX=""            # namespace in front of each metric name, when the store uses one
# QUEUE_METRICS_TIMEOUT_MS="4000"    # per-request timeout; a slow store degrades the page, never blocks it
